Report the BQ27220's status from its current (keyboard-base task 5.3).

The BQ27220 keeps FC (BatteryStatus bit 9) set after charge termination
until the state of charge falls below its clear threshold. bq27xxx checks FC
first, so the base's battery read Full at -410 mA and at +720 mA on the
board (docs/evidence/keyboard-base/charger/). For the BQ27220 only, a
nonzero current decides Charging or Discharging; FC still gives Full at
zero current.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
@@ -1951,7 +1951,16 @@
 		val_curr->intval = curr;
 
 	if (val_status) {
-		if (bq27xxx_battery_is_full(di, flags))
+		/*
+		 * The BQ27220 keeps FC set after termination until its charge
+		 * falls below a clear threshold, so FC alone reads Full while
+		 * the pack discharges or tops up. Trust the current's sign.
+		 */
+		if (di->chip == BQ27220 && curr != 0)
+			val_status->intval = curr > 0 ?
+				POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING :
+				POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
+		else if (bq27xxx_battery_is_full(di, flags))
 			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
 		else if (curr > 0)
 			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
